STEP 1: Install metrics-server (kind needs insecure kubelet TLS)
----------------------------------------------------------------
k apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server/releases/latest/download/components.yaml
k patch deploy metrics-server -n kube-system --type=json \
  -p '[{"op":"add","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args/-","value":"--kubelet-insecure-tls"}]'
k rollout status deploy/metrics-server -n kube-system
sleep 60
k top nodes
k top pods -A


STEP 2: What does a node have?
------------------------------
k describe node lab-worker | grep -A6 -E "^Allocatable|^Allocated resources"

Allocatable = capacity minus what's reserved for the system.
"Allocated resources" = sum of requests and limits of pods on it.


STEP 3: Requests drive scheduling
---------------------------------
vi deploy-req.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: hungry
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels: {app: hungry}
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: {app: hungry}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: c
        image: nginx:1.27
        resources:
          requests:
            cpu: "1"
            memory: "64Mi"

k apply -f deploy-req.yaml
k get pods -l app=hungry -o wide
k scale deploy hungry --replicas=20
k get pods -l app=hungry | grep -c Pending
k describe pod $(k get pods -l app=hungry --field-selector=status.phase=Pending -o name | head -1) | tail -3

"0/3 nodes are available: ... Insufficient cpu" even though the CPUs
are almost idle (check k top nodes). Requests are reservations.
k delete deploy hungry


STEP 4: The three QoS classes
-----------------------------
vi qos.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: qos-guaranteed
spec:
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: nginx:1.27
    resources:
      requests: {cpu: "100m", memory: "64Mi"}
      limits:   {cpu: "100m", memory: "64Mi"}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: qos-burstable
spec:
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: nginx:1.27
    resources:
      requests: {cpu: "100m", memory: "64Mi"}
      limits:   {memory: "128Mi"}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: qos-besteffort
spec:
  containers:
  - name: c
    image: nginx:1.27

k apply -f qos.yaml
k get pods -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,QOS:.status.qosClass


STEP 5: See the cgroup limits on the node
-----------------------------------------
NODE=$(k get pod qos-guaranteed -o jsonpath='{.spec.nodeName}')
CID=$(k get pod qos-guaranteed -o jsonpath='{.status.containerStatuses[0].containerID}' | cut -d/ -f3)
docker exec $NODE sh -c "find /sys/fs/cgroup -path '*$CID*' -name memory.max -exec cat {} \;"
docker exec $NODE sh -c "find /sys/fs/cgroup -path '*$CID*' -name cpu.max -exec cat {} \;"

Expect 67108864 (64Mi) and "10000 100000" (0.1 CPU).
Same files as Day 2: Kubernetes limits ARE cgroup limits.


STEP 6: LimitRange (defaults)
-----------------------------
k create ns team-a
vi limitrange.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: LimitRange
metadata:
  name: defaults
  namespace: team-a
spec:
  limits:
  - type: Container
    default:            # default LIMITS
      cpu: "500m"
      memory: "256Mi"
    defaultRequest:     # default REQUESTS
      cpu: "100m"
      memory: "128Mi"
    max:
      cpu: "1"
      memory: "512Mi"

k apply -f limitrange.yaml
k run plain -n team-a --image=nginx:1.27
k get pod plain -n team-a -o jsonpath='{.spec.containers[0].resources}{"\n"}'
   -> defaults were injected by admission

k run toobig -n team-a --image=nginx:1.27 --overrides='{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"toobig","image":"nginx:1.27","resources":{"limits":{"memory":"1Gi"}}}]}}'
   -> Forbidden: maximum memory usage per Container is 512Mi


STEP 7: ResourceQuota (totals)
------------------------------
vi quota.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: ResourceQuota
metadata:
  name: team-a-quota
  namespace: team-a
spec:
  hard:
    pods: "5"
    requests.cpu: "1"
    requests.memory: "1Gi"
    limits.memory: "2Gi"
    services: "3"
    persistentvolumeclaims: "2"

k apply -f quota.yaml
k describe quota -n team-a
k create deploy many -n team-a --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=10
k get pods -n team-a
k describe quota -n team-a
k get rs -n team-a ; k describe rs -n team-a | grep -i -m3 forbidden

Only some pods start; the ReplicaSet reports "exceeded quota".


